course: dictionary
lesson: 9576
title: Strategy: a plan to reach a goal
level: primary-5
stars: 0
explain: A strategy is a plan for reaching a goal. When you want to get something done, a strategy tells you what to do first and what to do next. «Ivy's strategy for winning the game was to build her army slowly and save her coins.» The clues are slowly and save: her strategy is the careful plan she made before she started.
explain: Strategy can also mean the skill of planning, for example in games. In chess, a player with good strategy thinks several moves ahead. «In a strategy game, think, but do not keep everyone waiting too long.» The words strategy game tell you this is a game where you plan, and the rest reminds you not to take too long over it.
explain: You will meet this word in many lessons. In maths you learn strategies for sums, like counting on or using doubles. In reading you learn reading strategies, like predicting what comes next or rereading a tricky sentence. Each one is a plan that helps you reach an answer or understand a text.
explain: Check your meaning by swapping it in. «The Art of War is a classic about strategy.» Try it: the Art of War is a classic about plans for winning. That still makes sense, so strategy fits.
fact: A strategy is a plan for reaching a goal, especially a clever plan made carefully ahead.
fact: Strategy is also the skill of planning, for example in games, sport or war.
fact: Maths strategies include counting on, using doubles, drawing a picture, making a list and working backwards.
fact: Reading strategies include predicting and rereading.
fact: A «strategy game» is a game where you plan several moves ahead, such as chess.
exercise: «The team had a clever strategy to score in the last minute.» What is a strategy? | A ball that is very heavy | A loud cheer from the crowd | *A plan for reaching a goal | A kind of cloud
exercise: Ruby says a strategy for sums is to use doubles. Which of these is a maths strategy? | Sleeping in class | A red pencil | Counting on | *Working backwards | Singing loudly
exercise: «Ivy thought several moves ahead in her chess game.» Which word names this skill of planning? | Speed | *Strategy | Noise | Luck
test: Which phrase names a game where you plan several moves ahead? | Party game | *Strategy game | Ball game | Quiz game
test: Reading strategies such as predicting and rereading help you do what? | Eat faster | Run quicker | Forget the words | *Understand a text
exam: What does a good strategy need before you act? | *Careful planning | Lots of luck and nothing else | Loud shouting | Closing your eyes
